QR ADV secret compatibility verification - 2026-11-04

Scope: pkg/whatsmeow/service/qr_lifecycle.go, the RotateADVSecret case in whatsmeow.go, and qr_secret_rotation_test.go.
Dependency under test: go.mau.fi/whatsmeow v0.0.0-20261102152715-54038813c47f.
All test containers were disposable, used --network none and mounted source read-only at /candidate.
Tests use synthetic QR references/secrets, repository/event fakes and temporary logs. No real session, persistent database, registry publication or deployment was used.

Command:
docker run --rm --network none --mount type=bind,source=<workspace>,target=/candidate,readonly -w /candidate nandocosta/evolution-go:0.7.2-nc.5-dependencies go test ./pkg/whatsmeow/service -run '^TestQR' -count=1 -timeout 90s
Output:
ok  	github.com/evolution-foundation/evolution-go/pkg/whatsmeow/service	0.052s
Exit: 0

Command:
docker run --rm --network none --mount type=bind,source=<workspace>,target=/candidate,readonly -w /candidate nandocosta/evolution-go:0.7.2-nc.5-dependencies go test -race ./pkg/whatsmeow/service -run '^TestQR' -count=1 -timeout 90s
Output:
ok  	github.com/evolution-foundation/evolution-go/pkg/whatsmeow/service	1.226s
Exit: 0

Also ran gofmt on the three Go files and git diff --check for the same scope; the check returned exit 0 with only Git line-ending notices.

New coverage: current QR republished after two successive renewals, remaining references updated, non-ADV fields preserved, caller-owned batch copied, same worker retained, QR count preserved for the same reference, coalesced renewals before publication, pairing winning over an in-flight renewal, late events after pairing, active passkey pause, stale generation isolation, no forced logout, and QR credentials absent from temporary instance logs.
The existing QR lifecycle tests also ran under the race detector.

This validates adapter behavior with synthetic events; it does not claim a real WhatsApp server sent companion_reg_refresh during testing.
